  <!-- Skip Link -->
  <main class="seo-page"><div class="seo-answer"><strong>Direct answer:</strong> Psychosis and schizophrenia at Mind Grace Neuropsychiatric Clinic are managed with antipsychotic medication, family psychoeducation and rehabilitation-focused follow-up aimed at preventing relapse and restoring function.</div>
<section class="seo-hero"><p class="seo-kicker">Psychiatric assessment</p><h1>Support when reality feels difficult to make sense of</h1><p class="seo-lead">Changes in perception, beliefs, thinking, behaviour, sleep, or functioning need a timely and careful clinical assessment, often with family context.</p><div class="seo-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Contact the clinic</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/emergency/">Urgent-help information</a></div></section><section class="seo-section"><h2>What may be considered</h2><div class="seo-grid"><article class="seo-card"><h3>Current symptoms</h3><p>The clinician may discuss what has changed, how quickly, sleep, health, medicines, substances, and daily safety.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Family involvement</h3><p>With consent and where appropriate, family observations can help build a clearer picture and support plan.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Referral needs</h3><p>Some situations need urgent hospital assessment or coordinated specialist care beyond an outpatient clinic.</p></article></div><div class="seo-note"><strong>Urgent safety:</strong> If there is immediate danger, severe confusion, or risk of harm, call 112 or go to the nearest emergency department.</div></section>    
  </main>
